{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "F6ScalarOnlyComponentHasNoTestableState",
    "description": "FINDING F6 (expected to FAIL at the pinned toolchain). A component whose variables are ALL scalars, and whose equations are all algebraic (no ODE state), has no assertable state under `esm test`:\n\n  assertion evaluation failed: scalar state 'answer' not found\n\nDeclaring a single array-shaped variable anywhere in the same component makes the identical scalar assertion pass -- the model then takes the array runtime, which materializes state-free observeds, instead of the scalar ODE path, which has no state vector to report.\n\nThis does not bite this repo: PLAN.md §1.2's convention is that components carry no clock, and the tables-stay-tables convention gives every MOVES component at least one column array, so every component is on the array path already. It is recorded because it makes the workaround PLAN.md §1.2 described -- adding a trivial `D(clock) ~ 0` state -- look necessary for a reason that is not the real one, and because it is a trap for anyone factoring a small pure-arithmetic helper component out of a calculator: the helper would be untestable in isolation for no reason the author could see.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"]
  },
  "models": {
    "ScalarOnly": {
      "variables": {
        "input": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 21.0 },
        "answer": { "type": "unknown", "units": "1" }
      },
      "equations": [
        { "lhs": "answer", "rhs": { "op": "*", "args": [2.0, "input"] } }
      ],
      "tests": [
        { "id": "an_algebraic_scalar_should_be_assertable",
          "description": "Should be 42. Errors with \"scalar state 'answer' not found\" instead.",
          "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.0 },
          "assertions": [ { "variable": "answer", "time": 0.0, "expected": 42.0 } ] }
      ]
    }
  }
}
